  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The conditional update identities and inequalities are supported under Q7, but equivalence of the complete law and reference domains is not established. The direct judge's affirmative classification treats explicit certificate premises as sufficient justification for their source applicability. That does not discharge the domain comparison required by the methodology. The adjudicated classification is undetermined.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target assumes routine.HasRiemannAccuracy errorBound before every conclusion. D016 expands this into existence of a D027 reference for every admitted problem. Q7 specifies independent old-average and physical face-flux error bounds and information-only routines, but does not expressly select all of D027's representative requirements or D025's ambient derivative requirements."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Independent inspection confirms the round-trip concerns are about the effective domain of the proposition, not an incorrect sign, missing computational composition, or compulsory returned exact field. The native supplements resolve the external-operator uncertainties identified by the blind translator, but do not establish the disputed source correspondence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D019 explicitly composes solve, extract, and numericalFlux. D023 subtracts timeStep/cellVolume times net outward flux. The native supplement identifies real volume through Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id and Real.volume_Ioc, the Bochner integral through integral_def and integral_eq, and the target norm through FiniteRealVectorNormEvidence.ring_norm_eq_sup and its norm-instance equalities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Undetermined remains appropriate after resolving the algebraic, operator, execution, and nonvacuity questions. No demonstrated mismatch warrants a categorical rejection as weaker or different, but the remaining domain questions prevent acceptance. A conditional theorem with additional applicability requirements cannot be classified as faithful-stronger merely because its conclusions contain more formulas.",
      "primary_evidence": "Methodology Section 2 distinguishes genuine strength from additional hypotheses and restricted types. The attached printed pages 4–6 provide the qualitative workflow and integral conservation context; the separate interpretations add conditional accuracy and rectangle conservation without completely specifying the target's law and reference classes."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The finite real vector representation, component indexing, space/time argument order, and two ordered interface problems are understood and appropriate. The precise nonlinear hyperbolicity domain remains unresolved: the declaration requires ambient Fréchet differentiability and a complete real eigenbasis at each state in S, including any boundary states S contains. The available primary-source pages do not establish that exact requirement.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 quantifies over every state in law.states. D025 uses HasFDerivAt, whose D171 body uses the full neighborhood filter, and D031 requires a real basis of eigenvectors. D176 represents the derivative by its standard-coordinate matrix. Printed page 5 invokes hyperbolic equations and linear eigenstructure but does not define the complete nonlinear differentiability domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C03 unclear",
      "resolution": "Witness order is sound: accuracy supplies a reference separately for each admitted problem, and each selected reference works for every subsequent comparison-bound triple. Neither uniqueness nor a reference returned by solve is asserted. However, the accuracy premise quantifies over the routine's entire admitted domain, whereas the update executes only two problems. Q7 does not explicitly establish this global certificate requirement as part of the selected local claim.",
      "primary_evidence": "D016 has the form forall problem admitted, exists reference, norm error <= errorBound problem. The target places both reference existentials before the final universal oldBound, leftComparison, and rightComparison binders. D028 imposes no relationship between Result and Reference. Q7 selects a local conditional error interpretation without specifying a domain-wide reference certificate."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Positive cell width and duration, explicit integrability, and the physical left-minus-right rectangle balance fit the applicable recorded conventions. Requiring conservation only during the reference horizon does not impose global-time solutionhood. The remaining issue is whether the stronger bundled reference assumptions, including literal endpoint fluxes at every spatial endpoint, are part of the adopted interpretation. Their presence as hypotheses does not itself settle that question.",
      "primary_evidence": "The physical target has four integrability premises and one rectangle equality. D027 requires spatial integrability at every time in [0,T], face integrability at every spatial point, and balance for all spatial endpoints and 0<=u<=v<=T. The inherited receipt adopts finite rectangle conservation with integrability, while the supplied scope rule expressly prohibits inferring pointwise representative conventions."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The conditional quantitative content is legitimate under Q7 and is not an unconditional accuracy or convergence claim. Arbitrary information types preserve approximate routines. Generalizing the physical field to one satisfying only the needed rectangle is harmless for the algebraic estimate. Nevertheless, that generalization does not compensate for unresolved restrictions introduced through Law and HasRiemannAccuracy. Complete equivalence of applicability remains unproved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target permits any q satisfying its four integrability premises and one balance, without state-membership or global PDE assumptions on q. It simultaneously requires D026's Law and D016's reference-based accuracy. Printed page 6 permits approximate Riemann solvers; Q7 permits independent error bounds but supplies neither the full Law definition nor an explicit domain-wide reference requirement."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Initial values at x=0 remain free, and positive finite intervals with explicit integrability avoid default-zero integral and inverse conventions. Positive-time representative dependence is real: D027 and D014 use literal field evaluations, not separately supplied flux traces. This is not automatically a mismatch, because the adopted rectangle interpretation may intend compatible representatives, but the supplied evidence does not prove that every intended reference admits such a representative.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 constrains only x<0 and x>0. D014 averages law.flux(reference.field 0 tau). D027 uses law.flux(field a tau) and law.flux(field b tau) for every a,b. For illustration, with scalar F(u)=u, changing the constant field W=1 to W(0,tau)=0 for positive tau leaves every spatial integral unchanged but makes the rectangle balance on [0,1] fail: its mass change is zero while its integrated endpoint-flux difference is -T. This establishes representative sensitivity, not failure of existence of a compatible representative."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Reference existence is assumed through accuracy, not inferred from hyperbolicity. Exact computational output, uniqueness, entropy selection, and global-time existence are not required. Joint nonvacuity is established with nonconstant interface problems and nonzero approximation errors. These facts resolve possible vacuity objections but do not establish coverage of the intended nonlinear reference class.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native declarations give admitted scalar transport problems (0,1) and (1,0), an information-only biased routine with bias 1/2, and actual_two_face_source_application. Independently, for F(u)=u the speed-one traveling steps have reference means 0 and 1; the biased routine gives numerical fluxes 1/2 and 3/2. With q=1, central state 1, and unit width and duration, next=0 and the update error is 1. Both reference errors are 1/2. This verifies a substantive satisfiable instance without proving universal reference representability."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The Lean target supplies the selected normalized update and both conditional error estimates wherever its certificate and admission premises hold. It preserves ordered neighboring inputs and the actual information pipeline. Whether it covers the entire source claim under Q7 remains unclear because the source-domain-to-certificate-domain correspondence is unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Writing dx=b-a and dt=t-s, the target asserts dx*(next-Q_t)=dx*(center-Q_s)+dt*((G_L-H_a)-(G_R-H_b)), with vector scaling understood componentwise. Its direct bound is oldBound+dt/dx*(leftBound+rightBound). These implement Q7, but all occur after HasRiemannAccuracy and the two admission premises."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Under Q7 and the applicable inherited rectangle convention, the algebraic conclusions follow once all target premises are supplied. Reference-mediated bounds follow by two triangle inequalities and the accuracy witnesses. This establishes conditional derivability, but not that the interpreted source selects the exact additional law and certificate premises. The full semantic implication therefore remains unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.10) has incoming left flux minus outgoing right flux. D024 divides by interval length, and D023 defines the conservative update. D016 supplies same-problem references and their error bounds; D027 supplies their initial data and rectangle properties. Neither the printed passage nor the recorded interpretations explicitly identifies the complete target reference and ambient-hyperbolicity domains."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation and the applicable inherited rectangle convention, the target correctly gives the local information/flux/update construction, normalization, conservation signs, and conditional error propagation on its effective domain. It allows information-only approximate routines and is nonvacuous. The evidence does not establish that the target's ambient-differentiability law class and domain-wide accuracy certificates using all-endpoint pointwise references cover the entire selected interpreted source claim. Acceptance cannot follow solely from correctness on the restricted domain."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under Q7 and the inherited rectangle convention, the update error identity and direct bound follow from normalized conservation and elementary norm inequalities. Given the target's accuracy premise, its reference witnesses and reference-mediated bound also follow. However, using that premise to derive its consequences does not establish source correspondence of its exact reference class, domain-wide quantification, or ambient hyperbolicity assumptions. Those requirements are not completely determined by the supplied source and scoped interpretations, so full semantic equivalence remains unresolved."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "Whether the intended hyperbolic-law domain requires ambient Fréchet differentiability with a complete real eigenbasis at every admissible state, particularly at state-domain boundaries.",
    "Whether every intended Riemann reference under the inherited rectangle interpretation admits a state-valued representative whose literal physical flux satisfies the target's all-endpoint rectangle equations and defines the interface mean at x=0.",
    "Whether Q7's local conditional workflow includes a reference-based accuracy certificate over every admitted problem, or whether that is an additional applicability restriction on the supplied routine.",
    "The printed passage itself does not specify the norm, error formula, tolerance, trace convention, or full weak-solution admissibility class. The recorded interpretations resolve only their expressly stated portions."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "reference-domain-correspondence-unresolved",
      "evidence": "D027 requires literal endpoint evaluations for all rectangles, and D014 uses the same representative at spatial zero. The inherited scope rule prohibits inferring pointwise representative conventions. Representative sensitivity can be exhibited even for scalar transport.",
      "impact": "The accuracy certificate's comparison class is understood as Lean mathematics, but its applicability to the complete interpreted source domain is not established."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "law-domain-correspondence-unresolved",
      "evidence": "D001, D025, D026, and D031 require ambient Fréchet differentiability and real diagonalizability on S. The attached source pages invoke hyperbolicity without establishing these precise domain requirements.",
      "impact": "This bundled premise cannot be declared source-equivalent or treated as genuine strengthening on the available evidence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "conditional-premise-scope",
      "evidence": "HasRiemannAccuracy quantifies over every admitted problem, while the selected update uses two calls. Its existence and error requirements are assumptions, not consequences of the printed workflow.",
      "impact": "Conditional derivability of the displayed conclusions must be distinguished from preservation of source applicability."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "operators-and-nonvacuity-resolved",
      "evidence": "The supplied native declarations identify normalized Lebesgue measure, Bochner integration, the finite-vector maximum norm, and matching integration/error norm instances. The two nonconstant transport calls with bias 1/2 give nonzero reference and update errors.",
      "impact": "No unresolved operator substitution, division degeneracy, compulsory exact returned field, or inherent vacuity explains the remaining nonacceptance."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I inspected the attached primary-source renderings and the supplied declaration evidence, including the direct and blind dossiers, translation, judgments, and native supplements. I did not access tools or independently recompute hashes. The conservation signs, normalized averages, ordered interface inputs, actual computational composition, conditional bounds, and substantive nonvacuity are established. The unresolved issues concern correspondence of effective mathematical domains, which provenance hashes and conditional proof obligations do not settle. The final classification is therefore undetermined, with no acceptance and no claim that the quantitative theorem is printed in the book."
}
